# Bash hook scripts must keep LF endings. Without this, Windows clones
# with `core.autocrlf=true` would silently rewrite the shebang to CRLF
# and break the hook on Git Bash / WSL. See .claude/hooks/post-edit.sh.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Windows batch files check out with CRLF. cmd.exe reads them in blocks and
# can miss a `goto` / `call :label` target in an LF-only file, so a clone
# made with core.autocrlf=false would break the launchers' error paths.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
